From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0390-upstream-01-mesh-points-and-lines.patch

Source: 0390-upstream-01-mesh-points-and-lines.patch
shader: EDEN_NX2_MESH_POINTS=1 compiles mesh programs that output points or lines

Port of Djihads80/Eglantine 743d5bbaed (Frizti, branch fix/oot-blackscreen, 2026-11-05).
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the core.

The source commit: Ocarina's garden hedges draw mesh programs with topology 0 (SET_MESH_SHADER_A
0x00040200, 32 points per group), whose pipelines failed with "Mesh output topology 0 is not
implemented" and whose draws were skipped. Points (0) and lines (1) now use OutputPoints /
OutputLinesEXT with PrimitivePointIndicesEXT / PrimitiveLineIndicesEXT. The map region holds one
index byte per primitive vertex. Point programs write the fixed state point size first. Its own note:
the pipelines build, the hedge leaves stay missing, their draws get a zero count from culling.

Changed from the source:
- Behind EDEN_NX2_MESH_POINTS=1. Unset, topology 0 and 1 are refused as today.
- Refused whatever the switch says with EDEN_NX2_MESH_AS_COMPUTE=1. 0180 reads 3 map bytes per
  primitive, keeps 3 corners each, draws a triangle list and hides unemitted primitives as
  degenerate triangles. A point would land on the wrong bytes and be drawn as a triangle. So 0180's
  "point and line topologies are refused earlier" stays true.
- 0052's clamp of each index below the vertex count stays.
- The point size constant is made only for point programs, so triangle programs emit the same
  SPIR-V as before.

Runs on the PS5: only where native mesh draws run, and those can freeze the console. Pool memory:
none. No cache version bump: the switch is off and a refused program was never saved.

Co-authored-by: Frizti <FriztiMouche@gmail.com>

